What this sheet does not carry: an oversized blurred gradient, a frosted panel, a glow, a stagger on load, an easing curve. When the user points at an effect like that, read it as a layer stack with `get-ui-principle({ topic: "reading-a-reference" })`. Label each claim Measured, Derived, or Inferred. Then rebuild it in the user's project from the owning principle, with these tokens.

This brand is flat: its tokens set no shadow or gradient, so they give you colour, font and radius but no material. Take the components from a catalog system: call `find-design-system` with the brand's look, pick a system whose scheme matches, call `get-design-system-kit`, then set that system's primary, font and radius to the brand's values below. Keep the brand's colour and type, and take the material of the buttons, cards and inputs from the system.","themeMode":"light","tokenCount":3,"tokensCss":":root {
